urg (German Cancer Research Center,  Heidelberg, Germany) for providing K<sup>d</sup>-transfected T2 cells.</p></fn><fn id="FN1"><label>1</label><p><italic>Abbreviations used in this paper:</italic> BFA<italic>,</italic> brefeldin A; endo H, endo-&#x003b2;-<italic>N</italic>-acetylglucosaminidase; ER, endoplasmic reticulum; NP, nucleoprotein;  PNGase, peptide <italic>N</italic> glycanase; rVV, recombinant VV; TAP, transporter  associated with antigen presentation; VV, vaccinia virus.</p></fn><fn><p>I. Ba&#x0010d;&#x000ed;k, H.L.Snyder, and L.C. Ant&#x000f3;n contributed equally to this work,  and are listed in random order.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>